X-SERVER-UNDER-BLINK status + decision (2026-05-29, ~36 CI cycles). The real Alpine Xvfb X server runs under blink IN-PAGE through every wall -- SOLID + unregressed (blink lanmower/blink@libblink-portabox 0ff15a8): (1) LLVM-OOM -> 49984B stub libGL; (2) epoll -> poll-backed epoll_shim; (3) display lock -> Xvfb -nolock; (4) listener socket() rejected -> finite RLIMIT_NOFILE (memorymalloc.c, fixes musl sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX)=-1); (5) AF_UNIX server sockets -> in-process unixsock_shim (socketpair-backed, abstract-addr aware) -- BOTH X listeners bind+listen; Xvfb reaches device init. LAST GATE = XKB keymap: Xorg runs xkbcomp via fork()+Popen which wasm cannot do. I built an in-VM synchronous fork+exec in blink (g_em_fork_stack, EmRunChildInline, SysFork/Execve/Wait4) but it hit LAYERED reentrancy failures over ~25 cycles: Xvfb startup daemonize-fork (no exec) breaks if fork returns 0 (exit 127) but tolerates ENOSYS; the keymap fork is nested (Popen->/bin/sh->xkbcomp); reentrant LoadProgram calls fatal exit(127). blink fork is now uniformly ENOSYS (proven-stable: Xvfb reaches keymap exit 1). DECISION (user): build a CUSTOM xorg-server/Xvfb from source in CI (Alpine abuild) GL-less + patched so the keymap loads a precompiled .xkm directly (no xkbcomp fork) and/or AllowEmptyInput makes keyboard-init non-fatal. Then launch X CLIENTS (xeyes/xsetroot, no keyboard) as SEPARATE top-level runElfs connecting over the in-process AF_UNIX socket (no guest fork needed). PRD subtasks: xorg-build A (rebuild xvfb musl + keymap patch -> containers/Xvfb-patched + server.xkm), B (gen .xkm, wire into X-smoke + sandcastle, witness client renders). KEY FILES: webix/.github/workflows/build-blink.yml (X-smoke), blink/{unixsock_shim,epoll_shim}.{c,h}, blink/syscall.c (SysFork ENOSYS + dormant vfork machinery), blink/memorymalloc.c (RLIMIT_NOFILE).